{% set guide = outreachSalesloftComparison %}
{% import "components/decision-guide.njk" as g %}
{% include "components/outreach-salesloft-schema.njk" %}
<main class="lp-page dg-page" id="simple-guide">
{{ g.hero(guide) }}
<section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('01','The useful differences','Outreach vs Salesloft:<br>what does each one do?','Compare the workflow, CRM connection and features included in the package you would buy.') }}
{{ g.table('Outreach and Salesloft: features, package differences and buying fit',['Buying question','Outreach','Salesloft'],guide.comparisonRows) }}
{{ g.sources([['Outreach packages','https://www.outreach.ai/pricing'],['Salesloft packages','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/Salesloft-Packages-and-Availability'],['Salesloft Cadence','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/Salesloft-Cadence'],['Outreach sequential dialling','https://support.outreach.io/support/solutions/articles/159000429165-configure-sequential-dialing']]) }}
<p class="sg-note"><strong>Salesloft’s package information is inconsistent.</strong> It lists Advanced and Elite, while an FAQ on the same page still mentions Premier. The written quote needs to settle what you get.</p>
<div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>Salesloft has the stronger HubSpot starting point.</h3><p>Salesloft documents two-way sync for people, accounts and opportunities, with activity logging into HubSpot. Outreach uses HubSpot Data Sync for contacts; its email logging runs from Outreach to HubSpot.</p><p>For deeper record sync, try Salesloft first. Test a reply, company change and opportunity update.</p>{{ g.sources([['Salesloft HubSpot sync','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/HubSpot-Admin-Guide'],['Outreach and HubSpot','https://support.outreach.io/support/solutions/articles/159000425625-hubspot-and-outreach-faq'],['Outreach contact sync','https://support.outreach.io/support/solutions/articles/159000426013-can-i-connect-outreach-and-hubspot-via-data-sync-by-hubspot-']]) }}</div><div><h3>Salesforce and Dynamics need setup too.</h3><p>Both vendors document Salesforce and Microsoft Dynamics connections. Permissions, field mappings and sync rules need an owner.</p><p>Salesloft’s Deals feature requires Salesforce. HubSpot and Dynamics buyers should leave it out of their value comparison.</p>{{ g.sources([['Outreach CRM connections','https://support.outreach.io/support/solutions/articles/159000426014-outreach-crm-connection-overview'],['Salesloft CRM setup','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/Manage-CRM-Sync']]) }}</div></div>
<p class="dg-related">Still choosing the CRM? Start with our <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">best CRM for outbound sales</a> comparison. For recording and coaching alone, see <a href="/resources/gong-alternatives/">Gong alternatives</a>.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="costs"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('02','Pricing and extra charges','Outreach vs Salesloft pricing:<br>what will you pay?','Neither publishes a complete platform seat price. Buyers should be able to check a starting price without a sales call. These published charges cover extras, before tax.') }}
{{ g.table('Published charges and quote-only costs; calling prices are additional to the platform',['Cost to compare','Outreach','Salesloft'],guide.costRows) }}
<p class="lp-small">Outreach’s rate pages show dollar signs without naming the currency. Confirm currency in its quote. Salesloft’s standard terms default to USD unless the order or invoice says otherwise.</p>
{{ g.sources([['Outreach Voice rates','https://www.outreach.ai/outreach-voice-pricing'],['Outreach AI overage rate','https://www.outreach.ai/pay-as-you-go'],['Salesloft Dialer rates','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/Dialer-Pricing-Guide'],['Salesloft billing terms','https://www.salesloft.com/legal/msa-2026-02-10']]) }}
<div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>Outreach can keep charging after credits run out.</h3><p>At the published overage rate, another 1,000 credits costs <strong>$1,400</strong>. Outreach says consumption continues after prepaid credits run out and bills the overage monthly.</p><p>Admin permissions and usage alerts need attention. There is no hard per-user credit cap in the documented controls.</p>{{ g.sources([['Outreach credit controls','https://support.outreach.io/support/solutions/articles/159000432352-can-i-setup-per-user-ai-credit-limits-or-is-it-total-account-wide-']]) }}</div><div><h3>Salesloft’s “unlimited” calling has a limit.</h3><p>Its fair-use threshold is pooled at <strong>3,000 minutes per licensed user/month</strong>. Five licensed users share 15,000 minutes. Exceeding the threshold in two months within a rolling year can trigger extra charges.</p><p>Get the excess-usage rate and destination coverage with the calling quote.</p>{{ g.sources([['Salesloft calling terms','https://www.salesloft.com/legal/product-specific-terms']]) }}</div></div>
<div class="dg-callout"><h3>Price the coaching setup you saw in the demo.</h3><p>For new implementations from July 2026, Salesloft’s conversation intelligence requires both Salesloft and Clari Copilot subscriptions, with the integration in the contract. Confirm whether your commercial quote bundles that cost.</p>{{ g.sources([['Salesloft conversation intelligence requirements','https://help.salesloft.com/s/article/Conversation-Intelligence-in-Salesloft?language=en_US']]) }}</div>
<p class="dg-related"><strong>Our view:</strong> walk away if the vendor will not give you an itemised first-year total. You should know what the purchase will cost.</p>
</div></section>
