<section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="alternatives"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('04','A useful price reference','Apollo, Close or lemlist:<br>could a simpler option do the job?','USD base subscriptions on annual billing. The first three columns show monthly equivalents. Calling usage, data, email accounts and optional features can add cost.') }}
{{ g.table('Published annual-billing subscription rates for one, three and five users',['Plan','1 user / month','3 users / month','5 users / month','5 users / year'],guide.alternativeCostRows) }}
{{ g.sources([['Apollo pricing','https://www.apollo.io/pricing'],['Close pricing','https://close.com/pricing'],['lemlist pricing','https://www.lemlist.com/pricing']]) }}
<div class="sg-brand-grid"><article class="sg-brand"><h3>Apollo: start with data and outreach.</h3><p>Professional combines contact data with sequences and calling tools. Data credits and advanced dialling affect the full cost.</p><p><strong>Our verdict:</strong> start here if you need leads and outreach together. If a sample misses your buyers’ phone numbers, add a better data source or choose another provider.</p><a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/">Compare Apollo and other data options →</a></article><article class="sg-brand"><h3>Close: put calling inside the CRM.</h3><p>Growth includes workflows and a power dialler. Calls and phone numbers add usage charges. Predictive dialling and live coaching sit in Scale.</p><p><strong>Our verdict:</strong> choose Growth for CRM-led calling. Leave Scale alone unless you will use its extra controls, predictive dialler or live coaching.</p><a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">Compare outbound CRM options →</a></article><article class="sg-brand"><h3>lemlist: combine campaign channels.</h3><p>Multichannel includes five email senders per user and an in-app dialler. Data enrichment and channel add-ons can increase the bill.</p><p><strong>Our verdict:</strong> buy it for campaigns that use several channels. For email alone, skip Multichannel and compare the Email plan.</p><a href="/resources/best-cold-email-software/">Compare email software and limits →</a></article><article class="sg-brand"><h3>Buying mainly for the dialler?</h3><p>If the problem is a slow calling queue, compare dedicated diallers. Test callbacks, voicemail and switchboards before paying for parallel calling.</p><p>A rep working a short, researched account list needs time to listen and take useful notes between calls.</p><a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">Compare dedicated cold calling diallers →</a></article></div>
</div></section>
<section class="lp-section" id="trial"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('05','Make the demo prove something','Test one campaign<br>from first email to callback.','Use a test contact you control. Ask each vendor to run the same short sequence in the package it has quoted.') }}
<div class="sg-flow"><div><h3>Send an email and reply.</h3><p>Check that the reply reaches the right rep and the next automated email stops. Show the team how to handle a referral or a request to stop contact.</p></div><div><h3>Make a call and set a callback.</h3><p>Use a call task, record the outcome and set a follow-up time. The next rep should see who answered, what was said and what to do next.</p></div><div><h3>Check the CRM and manager view.</h3><p>Confirm the owner, notes and next action arrive without duplicates. Ask the manager to find the call and review it using only the features in the quote.</p></div></div>
<div class="lp-note"><strong>Switching from an existing platform?</strong><p>Export a small sample of contacts, activity history, sequences and recordings first. Check what the replacement can import and which rules need rebuilding before moving the team.</p></div>
<p class="dg-related">A calling step needs a clear reason to contact the buyer. Prepare with our <a href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/">free cold calling scripts</a> and <a href="/cold-call-script-checker/">script checker</a>. If the team needs help delivering it, explore <a href="/services/sdr-training/">SDR training</a> or <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">managed SDR support</a>.</p>
</div></section>
